-- title:
--   Primitive narrow ray class character attached to a Galois character
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $M$ be number fields with $M/K$ Galois (no commutativity of $\mathrm{Gal}(M/K)$ is assumed) and let $\psi\colon (M\simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K]}M)\to\mathbb{C}^{\times}$ be a group homomorphism. Write $\mathfrak f=\mathtt{conductor}\,\psi=\prod_v v^{e_v}$, the locally finite product over the height-one primes $v$ of $\mathcal O_K$ with $e_v=\bigl[\psi\ \text{nontrivial on the inertia group at } v\bigr]+\lceil \mathtt{swanConductor}\,\psi\,v\rceil$, and let $\mathtt{localValue}\,\psi\,v$ be $\psi(\mathtt{artinFrob})$ for the arithmetic Frobenius at a chosen prime of $M$ above $v$ when $\psi$ kills the inertia group at $v$, and $0$ otherwise. Then there is a monoid homomorphism $\chi$ from the narrow ray class group $\bigl(\mathtt{coprimeToModulus}\,K\,\mathfrak f\bigr)/\mathtt{narrowRaySubgroup}\,K\,\mathfrak f$ — invertible fractional ideals with vanishing $v$-adic count at every $v\mid\mathfrak f$, modulo the subgroup generated by $\mathtt{narrowRaySet}\,K\,\mathfrak f$ — to the multiplicative monoid $\mathbb{C}$ such that: (i) $\chi$ of the class of $v$ equals $\mathtt{localValue}\,\psi\,v$ for every $v\nmid\mathfrak f$; (ii) $\chi=1$ exactly when $\psi=1$; (iii) for every nonzero $\alpha\in\mathcal O_K$ whose principal ideal is coprime to $\mathfrak f$ and with $\alpha-1\in\mathfrak f$, $\chi$ of the class of $(\alpha)$ is $\prod_w \operatorname{sign}(w(\alpha))$, the product over the real places $w$ of $K$ at which $\mathtt{IsPlusAt}\,\psi\,w$ fails, i.e. at which some infinite place of $M$ over $w$ has $\psi$ nontrivial on its stabiliser; and (iv) $\chi$ is primitive: for every ideal $\mathfrak f'\supseteq\mathfrak f$ with $\mathfrak f'\neq\mathfrak f$ there is a nonzero totally positive $\alpha\in\mathcal O_K$ with $(\alpha)$ coprime to $\mathfrak f$, $\alpha-1\in\mathfrak f'$, and $\chi$ of the class of $(\alpha)$ different from $1$.
--
--   This is Artin reciprocity for a one-dimensional Galois character together with the conductor–discriminant bookkeeping: the character $\psi$ of $\mathrm{Gal}(M/K)$ is matched with a narrow ray class character whose modulus is exactly the Artin conductor of $\psi$, with matching Frobenius values, prescribed behaviour at the real places and primitivity at the conductor. It feeds the construction of the completed Artin $L$-series and its functional equation, [`ArtinL.Abelian.exists_completedLSeries_functionalEquation_u0`](thm.html#ArtinL.Abelian.exists_completedLSeries_functionalEquation_u0), in the Langlands–Tunnell part of the argument.
